# The loader, driver, and validation layers the VK-2 proof runs against, pinned
# per platform. Changing a value here changes what the compatibility record in
# docs/vulkan_compatibility_record.md is a record of.
#
# These are project-local selections passed to one child process. Nothing here
# edits a shell profile, installs anything, or touches another project's
# environment. VK-4 promotes what this pins into the production native manifest
# and CI image; until then the proof names them itself.

# macOS. The loader is the standard LunarG one already on this machine; the
# driver is deliberately NOT the SDK's own MoltenVK, whose manifest declares API
# 1.2 and so cannot satisfy the accepted 1.3 minimum. The Homebrew MoltenVK
# 1.4.0 manifest is selected by absolute path instead, which is exactly the
# override the loader documents for this purpose. Overridable with
# HETOIMASIA_VULKAN_DRIVER_MANIFEST and HETOIMASIA_VULKAN_LAYER_PATH.
MACOS_VULKAN_DRIVER_MANIFEST=/opt/homebrew/Cellar/molten-vk/1.4.0/etc/vulkan/icd.d/MoltenVK_icd.json
MACOS_VULKAN_LAYER_PATH=/usr/local/share/vulkan/explicit_layer.d

# Linux, inside tools/vulkan-proof/Dockerfile.linux-proof. Mesa's Lavapipe is
# the pinned software driver D-10 selects; both paths are where that container's
# packages install them. The container installs eight ICD manifests and this
# names the one deliberately, so a run that found no Lavapipe would refuse
# rather than quietly enumerate a different driver. The manifest carries no
# architecture suffix: the Mesa this container resolves (25.2.8) dropped it, and
# a recipe written against the older `lvp_icd.x86_64.json` spelling refuses with
# the directory's real contents rather than falling back.
LINUX_VULKAN_DRIVER_MANIFEST=/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/lvp_icd.json
LINUX_VULKAN_LAYER_PATH=/usr/share/vulkan/explicit_layer.d
